== Notes ==
* Ironically, this item is unaffected by [[Luck]].
* On its own, this item is considerably worse at generating [[Card]]s, [[Rune]]s, and {{E|Soul Heart}}s than {{i|Crystal Ball}}; Fortune Cookie produces 1 per 7.4 charges on average, while Crystal Ball produces 1 per 6 charges guaranteed. However, with {{i|9 Volt}}, Fortune Cookie produces 1 per 3.7 charges on average, nearly twice as often as Crystal Ball.
** If you include the chance of trinkets generating, then Fortune Cookie will produce 1 per 6.6 charges, or 1 per 3.3 charges with 9 Volt.
* {{p|Dice Shard}}, {{p|Emergency Contact}}, and {{p|Cracked Key}} can be generated by this item.
* Using this item in a room with enemies, spikes, or other hazards can often make it difficult to see what is happening, as nearly half of the player's screen may be covered by a fortune. This can be circumvented by pausing the game and waiting for the fortune to disappear.

== Synergies ==
* {{Book of Virtues synergy|description=Spawns a green wisp on the middle ring. Each wisp gives Isaac +0.2 [[Luck]].}}

== Trivia ==
* [[anti:Fortune Cookie|Fortune Cookie]] originates from the ''Antibirth'' mod, and by extension, from the ''Community Remix'' mod for the flash version.
** In ''Community Remix'', it had a 4 room recharge time and would always give a fortune '''and''' drop a card or a soul heart.<ref>https://web.archive.org/web/20221115035837/http://platinumgod.co.uk/old/index.html</ref>
* This item is a {{M|Fortune Telling Machine}} counterpart to {{i|Portable Slot}}, which behaves like a {{M|Slot Machine}}.

